Dear Kiralee,

The function readmulti.nts is the correct one to use for .dta files - they are "multiple specimen format NTS files", even if there is only a single specimen data in it. See this wiki for more information: https://github.com/geomorphR/geomorph/wiki/Reading-NTS-files

This function will work if there is only a single specimen in the .dta file - I did that just this morning. So the issue I see that you are having, from the error message below, is not a problem with the .dta file but the way you are calling it.

"Error in scan(file = file, what = "char", quote = "", sep = "\n", strip.white = TRUE,  :
  'file' must be a character string or connection"

This means you are not calling your file name correctly, But without your line of code I do not know what is exactly the mistake.

Emma

