Hi Dean,

Thanks for this info. I have read the papers you suggested for looking into measurement error (including some more recent ones [e.g. Fruciano 2016] which suggest using MorphoJ to look at measurement error-although I'd prefer to stick to Geomorph for the entire analyses, if this is possible...). But after re-checking the wiki link it seems as though it doesn't matter that I've got a more complex design (as far as I am aware) since "The MS terms are SS/df, which take into consideration the number of times each was digitized, and therefore need no further manipulation". Furthermore, after reducing the complexity to just look at 2 replicates from a single set of images, I am still getting some strange results.

Am I right in thinking that, regardless of the complexity of my model, I should not need to change the following:

((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2) / (AOV$MS[2] + ((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2))

I conducted this both with and without semi-landmarks and got the following results:
with semilandmarks:
rep.er <http://rep.er> <- procD.lm(gpa.res.before$coords ~ Ind:Rep)
AOV <- rep.er <http://rep.er>$aov.table

                   Df      SS               MS              Rsq          F         Z      Pr(>F)

Ind:Rep     177   0.63192   0.0035702     0.52501 1.0991 1.0458  0.091 .
Residuals  176   0.57171   0.0032484
Total          353   1.20363

((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2) / (AOV$MS[2] + ((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2))

0.04719303

without semilandmarks:
rep.er <http://rep.er> <- procD.lm(gpa.res.noSemi$coords ~ Ind:Rep)

                      Df          SS                MS                 Rsq                 F             Z           Pr(>F)

Rep                1       0.00273     0.0027343       0.0022717      0.8015     0.69532      0.516
Residuals     352     1.20090     0.0034116
Total             353     1.20363

((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2) / (AOV$MS[2] + ((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2))

-0.1102112

and then with a more simple design:
rep.er <http://rep.er> <- procD.lm(gpa.res.before$coords ~ Rep)

                   Df            SS              MS                 Rsq              F           Z             Pr(>F)

Rep             1        0.00273     0.0027343      0.0022717    0.8015    0.69532     0.516
Residuals   352    1.20090      0.0034116
Total           353    1.20363

((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2) / (AOV$MS[2] + ((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2))

-0.1102112

Any further suggestions on where I could be going wrong (if I am right in thinking that MS terms are SS/df and therefore no need to do any further manipulation)?

Thanks,
Sam

