Hey Mike,

Just to clarify, this is the model that I'm using:

rep.er <http://rep.er> <- procD.lm(shape ~ Ind:Photo)
AOV <- rep.er <http://rep.er>$aov.table

                  Df      SS        MS             Rsq        F          Z        Pr(>F)

Ind:Photo 176 0.55962 0.0031796 0.52703 1.1206 1.0554  0.081 .
Residuals 177 0.50221 0.0028373
Total         353 1.06182

((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2) / (AOV$MS[2] + ((AOV$MS[1] - AOV$MS[2])/2))

0.05689096

Which is, as far as I can tell, is what is recommended (https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/geomorph-r-package/Cj_CfXzJtrw).

Is the model correct? If it is then it seems as if my measurement error is really high.... I was as precise as possible during the digitising and the photos of the specimens were also as best as one could get. Would averaging all 4 sets of measurements per individual be a good/acceptable solution?

Thanks,
Sam

